<title>BELGIUM: Tractebel completes Fimeuse merger.</title>
<headline>Tractebel completes Fimeuse merger.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian utility holding company Tractebel SA said shareholders of Tractebel and its unit Fimeuse voted at extraordinary shareholders meetings on Monday in favour of a plan to merge the two by the absorbtion of Fimeuse.</p>
<p>The merger becomes effective, retrospectively, from July 1996, Tractebel said in a statement.</p>
<p>Tractebel controlled more than 96 percent of Fimeuse following a public offer for its shares earlier this year.</p>
<p>The merger involves the creation of 10,920 new Tractebel shares which will share in company profits from the financial year 1997, the statement said.</p>
<p>Details on the practicalities of the exchange would be published in newspapers during January.</p>
